<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">swordmaster</ansi>

The Swordmaster is the neutral elite of the Duelist (rogue route; no alignment
asked). It turns a parry into a counter-blow, and the counter-blows grow
harder and more frequent. It needs a weapon that can parry.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Blade Dance       ripostes deal 50% more damage
  35 Parry mastery     +5 parry chance
  40 Disarming Riposte a riposte that is a critical hit staggers the
                       target, which loses its next action
  45 Twin ripostes     it can riposte twice a round
  50 Perfect Parry     once a battle, it parries the next melee blow
                       automatically
  55 Counter-strike    a riposte also leaves its target exposed for a
                       round
  60 Unbroken Guard    no riposte limit while it is above half health

A riposte is the answer to a blow the Swordmaster parries; the Duelist's once-
a-round limit is the one the ranks above lift. Perfect Parry needs a parry-
capable weapon in hand and turns aside a hand-to-hand blow, not a shot.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Rogue elite talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Shadow Footing (+5 Evasion), Razor's
Edge (+5% critical chance), Quick Hands (+15 opening action meter). Every
elite rogue may take them. See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.


